Do not warp the pointer to the window center when the Umbriel window switcher activates a window; focus alone is enough, matching the Niri branch behavior.

The switcher's Umbriel branch asked CompositorPlatform::focusCompositorWindow for a pointer warp, which resolves to Umbriel's window-focus-warp action and unconditionally moves the cursor to the center of the newly focused window after Alt+Tab.
--- a/src/shell/switcher/window_switcher.cpp
+++ b/src/shell/switcher/window_switcher.cpp
@@ -205,9 +205,9 @@
       platform.focusCompositorWindow(entry.windowId);
       return;
     }
-    // Umbriel's exact-id action preserves the switcher's pointer-warp intent without changing taskbar activation.
+    // Do not warp the pointer when the switcher activates an Umbriel window; plain focus matches the Niri branch.
     if (compositors::isUmbriel() && !entry.windowId.empty()) {
-      platform.focusCompositorWindow(entry.windowId, true);
+      platform.focusCompositorWindow(entry.windowId);
       return;
     }
